1
00:00:01,440 --> 00:00:02,270
YAAAAM!

2
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:08,970
YAH, MO!

3
00:00:09,053 --> 00:00:09,883
YAH, MO! YAH, MO!

4
00:00:09,966 --> 00:00:12,180
YAH, MO, YAH!

5
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:16,880
Yu-Gi-Oh! YH, MjisO!

6
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,100
It's time to do

7
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:16,680
The End

8
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,240
Too little, too late.

9
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:34,240
I already have four
Exodia cards in my hand,

10
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:39,280
and I have a strong hunch that my next card
is the final piece of my deadly puzzle,

11
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:41,240
Exodia's left arm.

12
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,320
Once I combine all five pieces,

13
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:47,517
I will summon the unbeatable
Exodia and claim an

14
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:50,720
automatic victory as well
as your dark magician.

15
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:53,337
Our satellite imaging indicates the rare

16
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:56,037
hunter's cards are coated
with an invisible ink.

17
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:57,117
Mark's cards!

18
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:00,082
That means he always knows
which card he'll draw.

19
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:01,500
Let it go, Mokuba.

20
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:03,897
But Seto, the guy's a menace.

21
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:06,477
First he hacks into your
database, and now this?

22
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:07,390
Come on!

23
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:11,457
Mokuba, I'm well aware of that, but
I'm willing to let him slide this time.

24
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:12,658
Sorry, big brother.

25
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:16,657
You made me Battle City Commissioner
so I could enforce the rules.

26
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:19,577
Give me one reason why I shouldn't
bust that cheat out there.

27
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:20,778
Because I need him.

28
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:24,700
This rare hunter may have
something I want, Mokuba.

29
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,030
Besides,

30
00:02:26,113 --> 00:02:30,842
I can't wait to see Yugi squirm when he
faces the same Exodia he used to defeat me.

31
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,340
It's my move now.

32
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:35,040
I place one card face down on the field,

33
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:38,338
and I attack with Chimera,
the flying mythical beast!

34
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:40,340
Demolish his stone statue!

35
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:44,040
You're left with one monster.

36
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:45,710
Hmm.

37
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:48,680
That doesn't matter to me.

38
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:50,120
You're done.

39
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:53,420
I knew that even you
couldn't beat me in one turn.

40
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:58,560
All I have to do is draw my next card,
and not only will I win this duel,

41
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:00,956
but I'll score an even greater prize.

42
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:05,920
First I won Joey's Red-Eyed Black Dragon,
and now I'll take your Dark Magician.

43
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:08,380
My master will be extremely pleased.

44
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:11,700
Bye-bye, Yugi.

45
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:14,220
Now I will draw the final.

46
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:16,120
Not so fast, Rare Hunter.

47
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:17,140
A trap!

48
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:18,510
What is it?

49
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:20,050
Time seal!

50
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:22,496
That stops me from drawing any cards.

51
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:27,720
And that means you can't pick
the final Exodia card yet.

52
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:30,620
This duel is far from over, Rare Hunter.

53
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:35,200
Hmm, a desperate move
for my desperate prey.

54
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,260
Whew, I thought Yu-Gi was a gonna.

55
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:41,120
My Time Seal trap will only last one turn,

56
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:43,791
so I've got to stop him with my next card.

57
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:49,797
I have to win this duel so I can start
figuring out the secrets of the past.

58
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:52,197
The fate of the entire
world depends on it.

59
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:54,817
Now, I can't let him draw
the fifth piece of Exodia,

60
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:57,037
and I can't just keep skipping his turn.

61
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:59,677
There's gotta be a card in
my deck that'll stop this

62
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:02,017
rare hunter from summoning
the unbeatable Exodia,

63
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:03,982
and I need to draw it right now!

64
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,620
I play Light Force Sword!

65
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:15,220
It will randomly attack
one card in your hand,

66
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:18,237
preventing you from using
it for three full turns.

67
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:21,240
And I'll aim for a piece of Exodia!

68
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:26,300
Oh, no!

69
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:29,137
I can't control which
card my sword will slash.

70
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:32,396
If it doesn't get an Exodia
piece, I'll lose the duel.

71
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,060
Go, light my sword!

72
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,200
Not that one!

73
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:42,200
You pierced Exodia's right arm!

74
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:47,920
The Rare Hunter only has three
Exodia cards in his hand now.

75
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:54,740
I'm not done yet, Rare Hunter
To wipe out your monsters,

76
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:58,740
I'll start by sacrificing
Chimera for Summon Skull

77
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:05,320
Summon Skull Attack with Lightning Strike

78
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:17,060
Well, all right Way to put that Kate
Clown on the endangered species list

79
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:20,617
You see, your Exodia may
be unstoppable as a whole,

80
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:23,577
but the five cards that
make it up are easy prey.

81
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:25,040
Now it's my turn!

82
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:32,800
Rare Hunter, you have no
monsters to defend you.

83
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:34,880
Looks like a whole new game.

84
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,597
What's with that guy?

85
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:46,960
He's just as nutty as a fruitcake.

86
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:48,240
A whole new game?

87
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,460
Hardly, Yu-Gi!

88
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:52,960
You really think you can
stop me with one card? I do.

89
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:57,184
A professional card hunter like
me is prepared for any situation.

90
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,040
Check this!

91
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:02,000
Swords of Revealing Light!

92
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:04,540
Oh, no!

93
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:08,920
Not the swords!

94
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:12,697
My magical swords prevent
your monsters from attacking,

95
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:14,780
so you can't touch my life points.

96
00:06:15,260 --> 00:06:18,025
And once your life force
sword wears off, Yugi,

97
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:21,120
I can use Exodia's right
arm and summon the beast.

98
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:26,997
I can't attack.

99
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:29,904
And that means you won't
deplete my life points.

100
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:33,900
Come on, Yugi.

101
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:37,767
You gotta get to him before he
gets that last piece of Exodia.

102
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:42,527
Seto, why are we letting
that keep beat Yugi?

103
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:43,980
Why not?

104
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:46,777
Yugi should have been
prepared for anything.

105
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:51,340
Besides, it's about time Yugi felt
what it's like to face Exodia.

106
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:53,880
It's my move.

107
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:57,500
I'll draw one card and end my turn.

108
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:02,197
Thanks to my Swords of Revealing
Light, that's all you can do.

109
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:06,757
You're reduced to watching your own duel,
unable to attack, unable to even move!

110
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:08,605
I should just end your misery!

111
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:12,157
Why wait for your magic
card to expire when

112
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:14,711
I can draw another right arm from my deck?

113
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:19,217
Exodia cards are so rare that most
duelists don't own a single piece.

114
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:20,897
But I have three copies of each,

115
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:24,568
which means there are two more
right arms waiting in my deck.

116
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:27,280
Hey, what's so funny?

117
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:31,080
Your deck's loaded down with
so many Exodia body parts.

118
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:33,837
The odds of drawing the
right arm are slim to none.

119
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:35,537
We'll find out, won't we?

120
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:38,277
Your mistake is that you're
relying on one monster,

121
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:41,889
but a good dueling deck requires
the right balance of cards.

122
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:44,717
And you're still a prisoner
of my life force sword,

123
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:47,447
which means I have three
turns to defeat you.

124
00:07:48,180 --> 00:07:49,757
Hmm, wishful thinking, Yugi.

125
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:51,020
It's my draw.

126
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:52,260
I knew it.

127
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:53,900
A second Exodia hit.

128
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:56,997
It doesn't help, but I've
still got the upper hand.

129
00:07:57,080 --> 00:08:01,080
And thanks to my swords of revealing
light, my life points are safe.

130
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:03,640
Come on, Youg.

131
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,140
You can do it, buddy.

132
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:09,853
You still got two turns to figure out
how to stop this card swiping freak.

133
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:13,340
I play one card face down.

134
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:18,800
And I summon Alpha, the Magnet
Warrior, in attack mode.

135
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:25,680
You forget about my
Swords of Revealing Light?

136
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:27,100
You can't attack.

137
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:29,637
I can't yet. Huh?

138
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:34,520
But once I destroy your swords, my
monsters will be let loose. You won't!

139
00:08:34,940 --> 00:08:37,337
And remember, your deck has a tragic flaw.

140
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:39,957
It's cluttered with so many
Exodia pieces that you've squeezed

141
00:08:40,040 --> 00:08:43,569
out room for other cards needed
to protect your life points.

142
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:47,697
You need more magic and trap
cards to destroy my monsters.

143
00:08:47,780 --> 00:08:50,700
But all you have in your
hand are Exodia cards.

144
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,617
And take a look in front
of you, rare hunter.

145
00:08:56,700 --> 00:09:00,740
I've already destroyed the
only two monsters you summoned,

146
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:05,198
leaving you without a single monster
to guard against a direct attack.

147
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:08,597
The only thing stopping my
monsters is your swords card,

148
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:10,327
a weak and temporary shield.

149
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:14,544
Once my monsters are free, I'll
begin attacking your life points.

150
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:16,230
Impossible!

151
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:18,697
You'll never break free
from my trap before I

152
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:21,800
summon Exodia and obliterate
you and your monsters!

153
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:23,160
It's over, Yugi!

154
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:29,231
You've left yourself wide open
for a direct attack, Hunter.

155
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:31,200
Yugi, take him down!

156
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:35,740
There's no way you'll summon
Exodia in time. You forget!

157
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:40,820
Your monsters are trapped in my Swords
of Revealing Light, and it's my turn!

158
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:43,357
I bet it's a duplicate Exodia card.

159
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,097
It makes no difference to me!

160
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:47,257
Your Light Force sword
will soon disappear,

161
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:51,697
allowing me to access all five pieces
of Exodia for an automatic win!

162
00:09:51,780 --> 00:09:54,200
But not soon enough. Hmph!

163
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:58,657
What if Yugi does discover some trick
to destroy my swords of revealing light?

164
00:09:58,740 --> 00:10:03,660
His monsters will devastate my life points
unless I block with a monster of my own!

165
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:08,038
Yugi forgets that each individual
Exodia piece is also a monster card!

166
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:11,600
So I can defend myself with
my double of Exodia's head!

167
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:16,605
I'll be protected and still have the
necessary cards in my hand to summon Exodia!

168
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:18,450
Hmph!

169
00:10:18,533 --> 00:10:21,197
I summon Exodia's head in defense mode!

170
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:24,780
Now, you can't strike my life points! Hmm.

171
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:29,117
That's exactly what I wanted
you to do, Rare Hunter.

172
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:32,440
Now it's time for me to
destroy Exodia. What?

173
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:35,300
You activated my trap card!

174
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:37,240
A costly mistake!

175
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,460
Chain destruction!

176
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,150
Ah!

177
00:10:45,180 --> 00:10:46,540
It struck my deck!

178
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:49,877
While it can't destroy your
Exodia head on the field,

179
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:52,960
It can destroy the ones in
your hand and your deck.

180
00:10:53,520 --> 00:10:54,420
Oh, no!

181
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:57,620
My Exodia heads... ...are gone.

182
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:08,500
All of your Exodia heads have been
eliminated from your hand and your deck.

183
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:11,580
And with no heads left to play,

184
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:16,080
you can no longer draw all five pieces
into your hand to summon Exodia.

185
00:11:17,140 --> 00:11:18,720
No, that's impossible!

186
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:22,900
He found a way to stop
the Unstoppable Exoria!

187
00:11:24,780 --> 00:11:26,760
And I'm not through, Rare Hunter.

188
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:30,860
I also found a way around your
Swords of Revealing Light.

189
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:33,700
Activate Dust Tornado!

190
00:11:36,180 --> 00:11:39,260
This trap destroys one magic card.

191
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:45,940
Shattering your Swords of Revealing
Light, which allows my monsters to attack.

192
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:53,860
Next I'll play Monster Reborn Revive
Chimera, the flying mythical beast

193
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:58,400
Chimera, destroy the final Exodia Head

194
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:10,460
Now your life points are defenseless
against my attack I play Alpha,

195
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:13,040
the Magnet Warrior And Summon Skull

196
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:19,380
Summon Skull's electricity raises Alpha's
magnetic attack power by 200 points!

197
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:25,360
Now, my monsters, attack the
rare hunter's life points!

198
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:35,960
Yeah, you, you won!

199
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:44,780
I can't believe it, Yu-Gi defeated Exodia.

200
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:49,318
He may have beaten Exodia, but there's
one card Yu-Gi will never beat.

201
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:51,320
And I'm the one holding it.

202
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:55,088
I'm heading to Battle City.

203
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:56,640
Hey, wait up!

204
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:58,377
I'm Commissioner, remember?

205
00:12:58,460 --> 00:13:01,342
I gotta go and make sure
no one else is cheating.

206
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:02,510
Oh,

207
00:13:02,593 --> 00:13:07,322
if you detect a duelist using an Egyptian
God card, let us know right away Yes, sir

208
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:14,080
Way to go, my man Thanks, Joey

209
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:18,020
Ah, there it is

210
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:22,117
I'm taking Joey's Red-Eyes
Black Dragon and your

211
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:25,420
Locator card You won't
need to find the finals now

212
00:13:27,300 --> 00:13:28,130
What's wrong?

213
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:30,696
Something's rubbing off on my fingers

214
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:33,100
All these cards are marked.

215
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:35,520
He was a cheat. Not anymore.

216
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,720
I lost.

217
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:41,340
I failed.

218
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:42,870
Me?

219
00:13:42,953 --> 00:13:43,783
Forgive me, Master.

220
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:46,780
I tried my best. No!

221
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:48,680
Please don't be angry!

222
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:56,900
No, Master! Don't! Please! Spare me!

223
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,430
Yugi!

224
00:13:58,513 --> 00:14:00,640
That wacko's lost is mine!

225
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,300
I've seen this before.

226
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,186
That's the Millennium Symbol!

227
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:08,320
We meet again, Pharaoh!

228
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:17,860
Remember me, Pharaoh?

229
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:20,120
Actually, perhaps you don't.

230
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:24,020
You were trapped in the puzzle
when I dueled little Yugi.

231
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:27,777
Congratulations on
defeating my rare hunter,

232
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:30,507
though he was the weakest
duelist in my crew.

233
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:33,822
My other minions will
prove much more formidable.

234
00:14:34,340 --> 00:14:36,940
Noog, what is with this freak show?

235
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:39,900
Farrah, I've waited for you for years.

236
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:43,540
Finally, after all this
time, I will destroy you.

237
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:48,680
I will not allow my other rare
hunters to fail me like this one did.

238
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:51,877
I have little time for
his kind of foolishness,

239
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:56,017
so I have taken over his body and
trapped his mind in the Shadow Realm.

240
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:57,740
I am in control!

241
00:15:03,700 --> 00:15:04,530
Yeah!

242
00:15:04,613 --> 00:15:05,560
This guy's creeping me out!

243
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:07,133
How do you control him?

244
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:11,540
Each of the Millennium items
contains its own unique power.

245
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:16,740
So mind control is a simple
task with my Millennium Rod.

246
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:19,020
No good can come from that power.

247
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:21,937
The events of the past
will occur once again,

248
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:26,200
and that same great evil will
return to threaten the entire world.

249
00:15:26,460 --> 00:15:29,107
He must be the great
evil Ashisu spoke about.

250
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:31,800
Allow me to introduce myself.

251
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:35,580
Remember my name.

252
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:37,730
Merrick.

253
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:39,370
Merrick!

254
00:15:39,453 --> 00:15:41,880
What is it you want from me, Merrick?

255
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:45,000
I want what belongs to me.

256
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:49,140
And I'll take it using the
strength of the Egyptian god cards.

257
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:50,557
Egyptian what?

258
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:56,080
But millennia ago, a trio of powerful
behemoths rampaged throughout ancient Egypt.

259
00:15:56,360 --> 00:16:00,360
These Egyptian god monsters spread
destruction throughout the world,

260
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:03,137
until the pharaoh sealed
them away for eternity.

261
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:07,897
But when Pegasus created dual monsters, he
resurrected these mighty beasts as cards.

262
00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:12,333
With these Egyptian gods, I can destroy
you and claim the power I deserve!

263
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:15,160
You'll never claim the Millennium Puzzle!

264
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:17,140
You misunderstand.

265
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:20,160
I want more than the power of the puzzle.

266
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:26,420
I want the pharaoh's power, the boundless
energy of the ancient ruler himself.

267
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:29,920
With it, no one will stand in my way.

268
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:34,940
I'll use the almighty magic I gain
to conquer and lead the world.

269
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:37,940
I will be unstoppable.

270
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:40,500
The end is near, pharaoh.

271
00:16:40,820 --> 00:16:42,100
It's my world now.

272
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:44,860
Not yet, Merrick.

273
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:50,000
I'm beginning to understand why Ishizu
asked me to participate in Battle City.

274
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:55,040
It's my destiny to stand between
you and the evil powers you seek.

275
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:56,500
And I will.

276
00:16:57,560 --> 00:17:00,960
Then your destiny is easier
said than done, you fool!

277
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:05,140
I can't let Merrick win, or who
knows what darkness will come!

278
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:08,305
He may possess the magic
of the Millennium Rod,

279
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:10,497
but I have the strength of my puzzle!

280
00:17:10,580 --> 00:17:13,520
I have to beat him, no matter what!

281
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:16,400
Pharaoh, your days are numbered.

282
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:19,740
So enjoy the game while you still can.

283
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:23,120
Because your reign is coming to an end!

284
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:28,160
Man, that was weird.

285
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:30,480
I knew that guy was a big creep.

286
00:17:30,780 --> 00:17:34,192
But who knew he was just a
front for an even bigger creep?

287
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:36,700
Here you go, Joey.

288
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:38,632
Take your red eyes back.

289
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:41,730
Nah, you.

290
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:44,280
You hold on to it.

291
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:45,837
It isn't mine to take, pal.

292
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:47,567
You want it fair and square.

293
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:52,237
Besides, the Rare Hunters have
collected tons of rare cards.

294
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:56,177
Their decks are totally souped up, so I
know that they're gonna be tough to beat,

295
00:17:56,260 --> 00:17:57,090
even for you.

296
00:17:57,620 --> 00:17:59,149
What are you saying, Joey?

297
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:02,817
I'm saying, one day you'll need all
the powerful monsters you can get.

298
00:18:02,900 --> 00:18:05,257
Plus, you can think of me
whenever you play my red eyes.

299
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:06,637
It's the least I could do to repay you.

300
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:10,417
See, during the Duelist Kingdom
Tournament, you taught me rules,

301
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:11,497
killer strategies,

302
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:15,756
and everything else that I needed to
know to help me get to the finals.

303
00:18:17,420 --> 00:18:19,637
I couldn't have done it without your help.

304
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:21,073
That's what friends do.

305
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:23,244
That's my point exactly, buddy.

306
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:27,165
You always have my back, so it's
time I helped you for a change.

307
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:30,535
That's why I want you to keep
my red-eyes black dragon.

308
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:33,582
I know it's gonna come in
handy for you sometime.

309
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:38,462
Besides, this means that a part
of me will be a part of your deck.

310
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:42,037
It's kind of cool knowing that
I'm helping you save the world.

311
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:44,767
Don't get me wrong, I'm
still in the contest.

312
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:47,900
And I still have the rare
card requirement covered.

313
00:18:49,300 --> 00:18:53,006
Well, actually, I guess technically
you have it covered, Yu-Gi.

314
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:58,458
See, Red-Eyes Black Dragon wasn't
the only rare card I had in my deck.

315
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:02,697
You gave me another rare card way back
when I first started playing Duel Monsters,

316
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:03,610
remember?

317
00:19:03,693 --> 00:19:04,523
The Time Wizard.

318
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:06,997
Yep, it bailed me out of
James at Duelist Kingdom,

319
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:10,021
and I know it's gonna save
my butt in Battle City.

320
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:15,557
You know, when you think about it, Yug,
both of our hearts are in our decks.

321
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:16,600
We're a team.

322
00:19:16,940 --> 00:19:20,460
Together, we won't let any
duelist feed us. It's true.

323
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:23,217
We'll whoop this Maricree
and his rare hunter

324
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:25,937
Goon Squad so hard they
won't know what hit him.

325
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:29,020
They'll be sorry they ever
decided to mess with us.

326
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:31,320
Thanks, Joey.

327
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:34,757
Joey, I'll take good care of
your red-eyes black dragon.

328
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,720
Don't sweat it. It's yours.

329
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:42,620
You are a true friend, Joey.

330
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:46,420
And together we can take on
any evil that comes our way.

331
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:48,560
Yeah, all right!

332
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:51,017
Which of you duelists wants a piece?

333
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:53,453
Just step up so Joey can knock you down.

334
00:19:58,180 --> 00:19:59,497
Watch yourself, Merrick.

335
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:02,777
Yu-Gi and I are going to be
trailing you every step of the way.

336
00:20:02,860 --> 00:20:05,507
The rare hunters have
become the rare hunted.
